# ==== T-FMT-D (R41) fill-pack matrix — TRAILING-COMMA axis.
#
# SUBJECT: this fixture asserts `gg fmt` OUTPUT (byte-for-byte, in
# `fmt_fill_pack_comma_axis`) — a bulk `gg fmt` sweep MUST EXCLUDE it.
#
# ⚠ THE REASON CHANGED IN 2026-08-16, THOUGH THE FIRST TWO ROWS DID NOT.
# `cm_fill` and `cm_over` used to be comma-free because a PACKED list has
# nowhere for a trailing comma to sit. Under the magic-trailing-comma canon
# they are comma-free because THE AUTHOR WROTE NO COMMA — a trailing comma is
# now the author's keep-this-exploded signal, so an input that carried one
# would NOT pack at all. The assertion is unchanged; the reason under it is
# not, which is exactly the kind of accidentally-green row Core #15e Q6 warns
# about.
#
# The rows (Core #12 — this file samples the `comma` axis ONLY):
#   cm_fill     fill-broken       NO author comma, so the formatter may pack;
#                                 the close follows the last element inline.
#   cm_over     over-width single NO author comma either.
#   cm_comment  comment-broken    the INTERIOR-COMMENT cause, ISOLATED: its
#                                 input carries NO author comma, so the comment
#                                 gate alone is what explodes it. (It used to
#                                 carry one, which made it a two-cause cell the
#                                 moment the magic comma landed.) The exploded
#                                 shape emits a trailing comma on output, as it
#                                 always has.
#   cm_magic    comma-broken      the MAGIC-COMMA cause, isolated: no comment,
#                                 and short enough to pack comfortably, so the
#                                 author's trailing comma is the only thing
#                                 keeping it exploded.
#
# RED source per row: cm_fill / cm_over are TRUE pre-fix REDs (pre-fix they DO
# carry a trailing comma on output). cm_comment's red is break-and-restore
# (make `emit_delimited_list` ignore its `Gate` and always pre-render — the
# comment is then re-parented out of the literal entirely). cm_magic is a TRUE
# pre-fix RED: the pre-change binary packs it to one line and deletes the
# comma.
void cm_fill():
    Vector[int] a = [111111, 222222, 333333, 444444, 555555, 666666, 777777, 888888, 999999, 101010, 111011, 121212, 131313]

void cm_over():
    Vector[int] b = [aSingleArrayElementIdentifierWhoseRenderedWidthAloneExceedsTheEntireLineWidthBudgetOfTheGorgetFormatter]

void cm_comment():
    Vector[int] c = [
        111111,  # first
        222222,
        333333
    ]

void cm_magic():
    Vector[int] d = [
        1,
        2,
    ]
